From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:57:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 314/333] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on Speak replies
 (0313)

Three reviewers and a live browser run found these, fixed here.

Repeats: a persisted final was spoken again after its preview because its text
did not start with the exact spoken prefix, a second message in one response was
silenced by a per-response done flag, and a second SDK final with no item id was
skipped. The hook now tracks the sentences spoken this turn and per-source
offsets (a live preview, or a run of SDK chunks after the last final), speaks
only sentences not yet spoken, and accepts a refetched final only for a response
streamed live.

Boundaries: an end mark as the last character of the text is no longer a
sentence boundary, so "costs 3." no longer splits before "5 dollars".

Sends: a send is a new user message or a growing pending queue, not a status
flip, so a stray status change no longer cancels speech or loses text.

Utterances: the speaker keeps every queued utterance referenced until it ends,
because Chrome collects an unreferenced one mid-speech and the speaking flag
stuck on.

Fast answers: the effort is lowered first and the old one stored only after that
succeeds; restoring leaves an effort the user changed by hand, keeps the stored
state when the restore fails, and applies late when effort levels arrive.
Read-only chats hide Fast answers but keep the trigger usable.

Menu: Voice and Speed hints wrap, Voice names the voice that will speak, and a
chat switch remounts the control.

Speech text: link reference definitions are skipped, spaced pipes read as
commas, and asterisks inside words and globs are left alone.

Added 2026-11-08.
